# DLB triggers — Devops Leading Brief

When the user message matches a trigger below, follow **`/DLB`** and **Read** the DLB skill in full (dual-resolve: `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\skills\devops-leading-brief\SKILL.md` if present; else newest `SKILL.md` under `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\plugins\` whose path contains `devops-leading-brief`).

## Engage when any

- `/DLB <id>` or `/dlb <id>` → **brief** mode
- `/DLB <id> implement` / `/DLB <id> and implement` / close variants → **implement** (infer inline vs Superpowers per skill; user may pin)
- `/DLB` or `/dlb` (bare — then ask for the card number)
- `load devops card <cardnumber> for context` → **brief** unless they also say implement / just do it / don't ask me
- `I want to look at devops card <cardnumber> please fetch it for context` → **brief**
- Close variants that clearly ask to **load / fetch / pull / brief** an ADO/DevOps **card** **for context** → **brief**
- “devops leading brief” / “DLB” with a card number → **brief** unless implement phrases present

Also engage **Orient Q&A** when, in a thread that already ran DLB, the user asks where to start or how to probe the loaded card — answer from context; do not change mode.

**Brief:** Enrich in the report; write thin brief file; stop. Enrich is not a gate option.  
**Implement:** current agent (inline or Superpowers per skill); then **offer** ship (message gate before any commit/PR) — do not auto-ship.

## When NOT to engage

- Casual mention of a work item without asking to load/fetch context
- `/dev-triage`, `/devops-card` (different tools)
- Halo-only browsing with no ADO card id
